The default text-dump command is built in a 48-character string from the
user's home folder and '/tx_dump' through an internal WRITE, so every
program aborts at start-up ("Fortran runtime error: End of record") when
HOME is longer than 40 characters. Use a plain assignment, which
truncates: the command is only a default that the esprc file can set.

--- a/src/common/startup.F
+++ b/src/common/startup.F
@@ -1145,7 +1145,7 @@
       if(unixok)then
         write(gxwdcmd,'(a)')'import -window root '
         tprlbl='Text dump'
-        write(tprcmd,'(a,a)') upath(1:lnblnk(upath)),'/tx_dump'
+        tprcmd=upath(1:lnblnk(upath))//'/tx_dump'
         exemlbl='Standard exemplars'
         write(exemfl,'(2a)') instpath(1:ln),'/training/exemplars'
         dfdblbl='Standard defaults'
